      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Following two recent papers [Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys., 2015, 17, 3196; Mol. Phys., 2015, 113, 1843], we perform a larger-scale study of chemical structure in one dimension (1D). We identify a wide, and occasionally surprising, variety of stable 1D compounds (from diatomics to tetra-atomics) as well as a small collection of stable polymeric structures. We define the exclusion potential, a 1D analogue of the electrostatic potential, and show that it can be used to rationalise the nature of bonding within molecules. This allows us to construct a small set of simple rules which can predict whether a putative 1D molecule should be stable."},
